{
  "name": "MAIN - Upscale an existing Image",
  "author": "Pfannkuchensack",
  "description": "Parent workflow: feed in an image + prompt, upscale and refine it with any model type. Target resolution is derived from the image.",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "contact": "",
  "tags": "main, parent, upscale, img2img, callable",
  "notes": "Pfannkuchensacks Workflow Package\n\nSame idea as the 2-pass main workflow, but without the text-to-image step: you\nsupply the image yourself.\n\nPick one \"UPSCALE REFINE - <model>\" sub workflow, drop in an image, write a\nprompt describing it, hit Invoke.\n\nThe target resolution is taken FROM THE IMAGE: image size x Scale, then rounded\nDOWN to the nearest multiple of 16. The rounding matters - several denoise nodes\ndeclare width/height as multiple_of=16 and would reject e.g. a 1000x667 source\nscaled to 2000x1334. That is what the six Integer Math nodes do:\n\n    target = floor(image_size * Scale / 16) * 16\n\nThe sub workflow resizes the incoming image to exactly that size before\nencoding, so the encoded latents and the denoise resolution always agree.\n\nDenoising Start controls how much is changed: 0.6 keeps the composition and\nsharpens detail, lower values reinterpret more.\n\nThe model is selected INSIDE the sub workflow and appears here as an extra field\non the call node once a workflow is picked.",
